), also list Porter nonstops from Toronto to Lisbon, but I didn't find that confirmed for the coming season. Schedules change, so check before booking.\n\n**Cost in March:** Today is November 18, 2026, so I'm assuming you mean March 2027. I couldn't find a clean March 2027 fare table. The best March-specific data is from Air Canada's fare listings, which are round-trip economy fares and mix cash with points:\n- Feb 25 – Mar 30, 2027: from about CAD 306 plus 65,448 points\n- Feb 26 – Mar 30, 2027: from about CAD 306 plus 67,614 points\n- Feb 25 – Mar 1, 2027: from about CAD 251 plus 65,688 points\n\nThe [Air Canada page](https://www.aircanada.com/en-ca/flights-from-toronto-to-lisbon) also shows a lowest cash fare from CAD 663. These fares were collected recently but may no longer be available.\n\nOther estimates vary a lot. [Booking.com](https://www.booking.com/flights/route/city-to-city/ca-toronto-to-pt-lisbon.html) gives an average round-trip price of $1,245 based on bookings from the past six months, with a predicted lowest round-trip of $469. [TAP's site](https://www.flytap.com/en_us/flights-from-toronto-to-lisbon) shows a January 2027 round trip from US$434, but I didn't see a February or March 2027 fare there.\n\n**Rough expectation:** Expect a round trip from about CAD 500 to 1,250 in March, depending on the airline, dates, and whether you pay cash or points. The cheapest fares tend to be on Air Canada or TAP, and late-March dates often show lower prices. Confirm the final price on each airline's site."}]},"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1608,"cache_read_input_tokens":11481,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1478},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","refusal_category":null}]}
